From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:12:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] target/riscv: a version 11 cpu state still loads

QEMU 11.1.2 (stable commit 0d4875d, "target/riscv/kvm: Preserve MP state
across migration", a cherry-pick of ddac7cf) raised vmstate_riscv_cpu's
version_id and minimum_version_id from 11 to 12, for a new pre_load hook
and a KVM-only MP-state subsection. The fields did not change. With the
minimum at 12, every riscv snapshot saved by 11.1.0 fails to load:

    error while loading state for instance 0x0 of device 'cpu':
    cpu: incoming version_id 11 is too old for local minimum version_id 12

That is every riscv64 qcow2 snapshot and every record/replay start
snapshot made before the bump. Accept version 11 again. A version 11
stream has the same fields and no MP-state subsection; pre_load clears
kvm_mp_state_loaded as for any stream without it, so KVM keeps the reset
MP state, which is what 11.1.0 did.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Origin: new
---
 target/riscv/machine.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/riscv/machine.c b/target/riscv/machine.c
index 31c49ca3e6a15757f90672ec425fc38480254cb9..8d5df05bb46e5ae4dc611449836506ef47d66a55 100644
--- a/target/riscv/machine.c
+++ b/target/riscv/machine.c
@@ -499,7 +499,12 @@ static const VMStateDescription vmstate_mseccfg = {
 const VMStateDescription vmstate_riscv_cpu = {
     .name = "cpu",
     .version_id = 12,
-    .minimum_version_id = 12,
+    /*
+     * Version 12 added only the KVM MP-state subsection and a pre_load
+     * hook; the fields are those of version 11, so a version 11 stream
+     * (a snapshot saved by QEMU 11.1.0) still loads.
+     */
+    .minimum_version_id = 11,
 #ifdef CONFIG_KVM
     .pre_load = riscv_cpu_kvm_pre_load,
 #endif
